    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2023 was the soft year, revenue growth of 6.9% as More Personal Computing declined on Windows and Devices [D311][P39]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Microsoft Cloud reached $214.4 billion, 64.6% of revenue, and contributed 16.2pp of FY2026's growth [S24][D566][D568]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Server products and cloud services rose 31.5% to $129.4 billion, 39.0% of revenue, on Azure demand across all workloads [S61][D640][D641][P12]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Microsoft 365 Commercial products and cloud services added $14.2 billion, up 16.2%, on Copilot and E5 revenue per user [S64][D648][P14]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating costs grew 7.4% against 17.8% revenue growth, an incremental operating margin of 53.3% [D491][D472][D498]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS grew 31.6% against 31.3% net income growth, with the share count down only 0.2% [D476][D474][D493]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin of 46.8% is a window high, 5.1pp above the 41.7% median and 16.7pp above the FY2017 low [F50][D974][D975][D973]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin slipped 0.9pp to 67.9%, below its 68.2% median, as AI infrastructure investment raised cost of revenue [D486][F30][D981][P11]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Cost of revenue took 0.9pp off operating margin in FY2026, offset by R&D and other lines adding 0.8pp and 1.2pp [D500][D501][D502]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2026 net margin jump of 4.2pp to 40.3% came largely from $10.7 billion of other income, including OpenAI dilution gains [D488][F70][X124][P7]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Operating cash flow rose 34.4% to $182.9 billion, 55.1% of revenue, on higher customer cash and lower tax payments [F100][D477][D457][P1]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow fell 6.5% to $67.0 billion, a 20.2% margin and window low, as capex rose 79.6% to $115.9 billion [F120][D478][D456][D982][F110][D479]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow covered only 0.50x of net income, against a 0.91x median, and capex ran 3.38x D&A [D460][D990][D461]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The capex step-up reflects AI infrastructure build-out, with investing outflow of $139.5 billion including $51.4 billion more property additions [F130][P1]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Net cash was $72.9 billion, 22.0% of revenue, with total debt down to $40.3 billion [D465][D466][D464]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "That net cash position ranks in the 83rd percentile of six software peers, whose median is -7.2% of revenue [D1006][D1007]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Buybacks and dividends of $48.7 billion absorbed 72.7% of free cash flow [D467][D468]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The current ratio of 1.23x is a window low against a 1.93x median, as current liabilities compounded at 13.1% [F200][D991][D993][F233]."}
